  "gloss": "whenever, if (always)",
  "title": "と — whenever, if (always)",
  "pattern": "plain present + と、B",
  "explanation": "After a verb or adjective in the plain present, と means \"whenever\", or \"if… then (always)\": {春|はる}になると、{暖|あたた}かくなる — when spring comes, it gets warm. It’s for things that follow automatically: nature, machines, habits, directions. (A different と from the \"and\" between nouns.)",
  "natural": "Directions and how things work: まっすぐ{行|い}くと、{駅|えき}があります — go straight and you’ll come to the station. Fine in any register.",
  "stiff": "Not for your own plans, requests or invitations. \"If you have time, let’s meet\" needs たら: {時間|じかん}があったら{会|あ}おう. With と it sounds wrong.",
